  "notes": [
    "Manuscript page 3; pencil foliation 365. The page relates cohomology operations to cohomology of K(F_p,n), defines stability through suspension, and records the odd-prime Steenrod generators, their degrees and the name of the Adem relations. A bibliography in the lower left names Cohomology operations, Steenrod + Epstein, Ann of Math Studies N°50, Princeton, p77; no external source was consulted.",
    "The first displayed dual is literally H_* dual while the right side has fixed degree n+r. No degree subscript was silently supplied. The small K sequence and the lower left group omit a closing parenthesis as recorded. The lower P labels have isolated raised ticks, read as primes, not the mathematically tempting i. The top row of the suspension square uses flat bars and the bottom row waved tildes: the intended reduced-cohomology notation does not justify making their drawn marks identical.",
    "Degree accounting for the square was checked: suspension raises both n and n+r by one; the arrow labels are P_n and P_{n+1}. This check directs attention to the indices but is not a proof of the stability or generation assertions. There is no explicit authorial “à vérifier” on this sheet."
  ],
  "hand": [
    "K has a flattened upper arm and can resemble π or κ. All nine relevant marked occurrences on this page are consistent with K; the open K below the fold anchors the identification. C doubted K/κ at each; H used K. This is a page-local pattern, to be rechecked on later sheets.",
    "Reduced-cohomology marks vary in shape within one square: two short flat bars above, two waves below. C left the upper pair doubtful; H regularized them to tildes. The distinction is preserved, not asserted to carry different mathematical meanings.",
    "A small r is angular and can look like 2. Here r in n+r and the degree heading has the same form. The isolated raised ticks on P are provisionally primes (medium confidence), not a general rule for later i exponents."
  ],
